  "sections": {
    "1": {
      "purpose": "This System Requirement Specification (SRS) defines the system-level requirements for the telemetry acquisition subsystem of the [Project Name] R&D project. This subsystem is designed to acquire and process telemetry data from various sensors, supporting critical operations within the [Project Name] program. The intended audience for this SRS includes software engineers, system architects, testers, and other stakeholders involved in the development and deployment of the telemetry acquisition subsystem.\n\nThe telemetry acquisition subsystem will support the following parent systems: [List Parent Systems].  This document outlines the functional and non-functional requirements that must be met to ensure successful operation of the subsystem.",
      "scope": "Scope\n\nThis System Requirement Specification (SRS) defines the system-level requirements for the Telemetry Acquisition Subsystem.  The subsystem is responsible for acquiring telemetry data from various sensors, timestamping each sample, buffering data before flow control, exposing acquired samples through a REST interface to the ground segment, and recording an engineering log.\n\nIn Scope:\n\nAcquiring telemetry data from at least 3 sensor channels simultaneously (REQ-0001)\nTimestamping every acquired sample with a system time reference accurate to +/- 1 ms (REQ-0003)\nBuffering at least 10,000 samples per channel before flow control is applied (REQ-0004)\nExposing acquired samples through a REST interface to the ground segment (REQ-0005)\nRecording an engineering log with a minimum depth of 6 months of mission operations (REQ-0002)\nMaintaining a mean time between failures (MTBF) of not less than 2000 hours (REQ-0002)\nSustaining a sample ingestion rate of at least 100 Hz per channel (REQ-0007)\nRestricting access to acquisition controls to authenticated operators only (REQ-0008)\nCompleting a software restart in less than 30 seconds after a fault (REQ-0009)\nOperating within a 28 V DC power envelope not exceeding 45 W (REQ-0010)\n\nOut of Scope:\n\nDetailed design specifications for the subsystem.\nSpecific sensor integration details and calibration procedures.\nReal-time performance analysis and optimization beyond basic requirements.\nSecurity protocols beyond authentication of acquisition controls.",
