    "2": {
      "system_context": "System Overview\n\nSystem Boundaries:\n\nThe system under development is responsible for acquiring, timestamping, buffering, and transmitting telemetry data from at least three sensor channels. It interfaces with the ground segment via a REST interface to provide acquired samples. The system also maintains an engineering log of mission operations for at least six months.\n\nExternal Interfaces:\n\nSensor Channels:  The system directly interacts with at least three sensor channels, acquiring telemetry data from each channel simultaneously. (REQ-0001)\nGround Segment: The system exposes acquired samples through a REST interface to the ground segment for further processing and analysis. (REQ-0005)\nEngineering Log:  The system records an engineering log with a minimum depth of six months of mission operations, capturing critical operational data. (REQ-0006)\n\nSystem Context:\n\nThe system operates within a 28 V DC power envelope not exceeding 45 W. This constraint ensures the system's energy consumption remains manageable and sustainable for extended periods.  (REQ-0010)\n\nNotes:\n\nThe system is designed to acquire telemetry data from multiple channels simultaneously, ensuring comprehensive data capture.\nThe system timestamps each acquired sample with a system time reference accurate to +/- 1 ms, enabling precise temporal analysis of the collected data.\nThe system employs buffer storage for at least 10,000 samples per channel before applying flow control. This buffering mechanism ensures timely and efficient data transfer while maintaining temporal integrity. (REQ-0003)\nThe system's REST interface provides a standardized and accessible method for transmitting acquired samples to the ground segment.  (REQ-0005)\nThe system maintains an engineering log with a minimum depth of six months, ensuring historical data is readily available for analysis and troubleshooting. (REQ-0006)\nThe system's Mean Time Between Failures (MTBF) must be at least 2000 hours to ensure reliable operation in demanding environments.  (REQ-0002)\nThe system's sample ingestion rate per channel must maintain a minimum of 100 Hz, ensuring timely data acquisition and processing. (REQ-0007)\nAccess to acquisition controls is restricted to authenticated operators only, enhancing security and preventing unauthorized manipulation.  (REQ-0008)\nThe system's fault recovery process must complete a software restart within 30 seconds, minimizing downtime and ensuring rapid operational restoration. (REQ-0009)",
      "system_architecture": "System Overview\n\nThe system is designed to acquire telemetry data from multiple sensor channels simultaneously, timestamp each sample with high accuracy, buffer samples before flow control, and expose acquired data through a REST interface for ground segment access.  Additionally, the system must meet specific non-functional requirements including MTBF, sample ingestion rate, restricted access, fault recovery time, and power envelope constraints.\n\nNote: Detailed design information is provided in the System Design Document (SDD).",
